| F1 | open | BLOCKING | js/common/reviewSpecClaims.js | 🚨 blocking the anchor free word match keeps false claims blocking and mints a fabricated citation — reproducible with any short ticket line heading bullet wordoverlap js common reviewspecclaims js 310 uses the overlap coefficient alone inter math min claimwords linewords for a 1–2 word ticket line the denominator is the line so any line whose few content words all appear in the claim scores 1 0 ≥ ticket word match min overlap 0 6 js common reviewspecclaims js 241 and claimlinematch js common reviewspecclaims js 326 329 confirms it without any anchor markdown tickets are full of 1–2 word lines headings bullets so a claim the ticket never makes is verified reproduced end to end through the production sanitizer node current head text ticket md payment service error handling retries use exponential backoff with a 5 second cap claim uncited spec claim according to the ticket error handling must redact card numbers from every log line ← the ticket never says this sanitizereviewdata with tickettext downgrades 0 severity kept blocking census blocking 1 recommendation request changes citation minted path src payment js line 42 citation ticket md 3 posted body 🚨 blocking according to the ticket error handling must redact card numbers source ticket md 3 — requirement verified against the ticket text gh 1334 citation auto append ticket md 3 is just the heading error handling — the auto appended requirement verified against the ticket text line is false evidence downstream triage and the machine treat it as ground truth the census holds and rework arms on a possibly green pr — exactly the gh 1053 pathology but now with a citation that looks authoritative and is harder to disprove a bullet fixture fails the same way claim idempotency keys must rotate daily and be stored hashed is confirmed by the bare line idempotency keys citation ticket md 3 note the sibling function in this same repo already documents this exact failure mode and guards against it — js common findingregistry js 205 206 jaccard alone punishes subset paraphrases the overlap coefficient alone overates tiny sets — which is why claimsimilarity uses the mean of jaccard and overlap suggested fix validated against this pr s own fixtures gate the anchor free path on the line s content word count — a line must itself be requirement shaped to confirm a claim on words alone javascript function claimlinematch claimwords normalizedline lineno anchorcount var overlap wordoverlap claimwords findingregistry contentwords normalizedline var matched anchorcount 0 overlap ticket anchor min word overlap overlap ticket word match min overlap findingregistry contentwords normalizedline length ticket min claim words with the floor both repro claims fall to no anchor unseen anywhere ≥3 claim words → confidently absent → demote as today while every existing matchclaiminticket fixture still passes ac1 ac4 lines carry 9 content words the best line fixtures 7–9 and the near identical no anchor fixture 9 consider floored line length for the anchored path too a bare 401 on a 2 word line still passes today js common reviewspecclaims js 328 — at minimum please add a negative test pinning a 1–2 word ticket line never confirms an anchor free claim |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | js/common/reviewSpecClaims.js | 💡 suggestion stale contract doc — a demoted verdict can never carry claimmatchedticket yes the rewritten docstring of classifyfindingseverity js common reviewspecclaims js 454 456 documents the demoted branch as text demoted → claimmatchedticket yes no inconclusive yes here means the anchor was seen but the line did not qualify — that value is unreachable ticketmatchverdict js common reviewspecclaims js 366 374 returns yes only when a line actually matched scan best and verifiedordemotedverdict js common reviewspecclaims js 443 456 maps yes to the claimverified keep blocking branch the anchor seen but the line did not qualify case returns inconclusive scan anchorseen → inconclusivematch so a demotion can only ever carry no or inconclusive this module is a machine parsed contract the marker payload and the registry read these values — please correct the doc so future consumers don t implement against an impossible state |
