| F4 | open | SUGGESTION | js/postPRReviewComments.js | 💡 suggestion registryclaimof truncates reviewer claims that legitimately contain a horizontal rule registryclaimof js postprreviewcomments js 1057 1059 strips the machine appended demotion tail by splitting on the generic separator javascript return string claim split n n 0 the demotion tail is n downgradenote where downgradenote starts with n — so splitting on n n works for machine output but it applies to every claim including clean ones a reviewer authored multi paragraph claim containing a markdown horizontal rule n n loses everything after the rule in the registry identity — similarity for cross round dedup is then computed on truncated text weakening gh 1332 matching stripping only the known machine tail would be precise and loss free cut at the first occurrence of n n⚠️ severity demoted or of the dmtools demoted from blocking marker prefix already exported as reviewspecclaims demotion marker prefix edge case — identity matching only no posting impact the new tests pin only the demotion tail shape |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

