💡 **SUGGESTION: `applyCitationAppend` silently drops the citation when the comment file already carries a rewrite**

`applyCitationAppend` (js/common/reviewSpecClaims.js:573) ignores `planRewrite`'s return value:

```javascript
} else if (resolved.fromFile && c.comment) {
    planRewrite(out, c.comment, appendCitationToBody(resolved.body, citation));
}
out.citations.push({ path: target, line: c.line || null, citation: citation });
out.notes.push('inline comment on ' + target + ' kept BLOCKING: claim verified against ' + citation + ...');
```

`planRewrite` is first-wins per physical comment file (the demotion dedupe — documented for demotions). If two inline entries reference the same comment file and the **first** is demoted (rewrite planned) while the **second** verifies, the verified entry's citation is recorded in `out.citations`, logged `✅ gh-1334 spec-claim verified ... citation auto-appended` — but the posted file content never receives the `Source:` line. Two *verified* entries on one file have the same shape (second citation dropped).

Edge shape only (two inline entries → one physical comment file), no census impact. Consider skipping the ✅ log (or emitting a note) when `planRewrite` returns `false`, so the log doesn't claim an append that didn't happen.

💡 **SUGGESTION: `loadSpecClaimsWithRegistry` duplicated verbatim across two test files**

The identical 12-line helper is copy-pasted into `js/unit-tests/test_postStoryTestAutomationReview.js` and `js/unit-tests/test_postStoryTestAutomationReviewHelpers.js` (same comment, same body):

```javascript
function loadSpecClaimsWithRegistry() {
    return loadModule('js/common/reviewSpecClaims.js', makeRequire({
        './findingRegistry.js': loadModule('js/common/findingRegistry.js', makeRequire({
            './machineAuthor.js': machineAuthorReal(),
            './reviewVerdicts.js': reviewVerdictsReal()
        }))
    }), {});
}
```

The comment in both says "the same way the shared loaders in test_postPRReviewComments.js do" — a third copy concept that already lives in shared loaders. When the `findingRegistry.js` require graph changes again, all copies must be edited in lockstep. Consider moving it into the shared loader module the two files already import from. Test-only, no runtime impact.

